1
00:00:48,860 --> 00:00:52,890
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,340 --> 00:00:55,950
[Episode 2]

3
00:00:56,090 --> 00:00:59,320
[The People's Railway Serves the People]

4
00:00:59,930 --> 00:01:01,590
"This is my daughter, Qianqian.

5
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:06,810
I've run into some trouble
with my business lately.

6
00:01:06,810 --> 00:01:07,950
You're kind-hearted.

7
00:01:07,950 --> 00:01:09,250
I know you'll help.

8
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:11,200
Take good care of this kid.

9
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:14,710
Once I sort things out, I'll come

10
00:01:14,710 --> 00:01:15,920
pick her up as soon as I can.

11
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:17,900
Thank you so much."

12
00:01:24,570 --> 00:01:25,770
Can you believe this guy?

13
00:01:25,930 --> 00:01:26,710
Back when we got divorced,

14
00:01:26,710 --> 00:01:27,590
we fought like cats and dogs.

15
00:01:27,590 --> 00:01:28,860
He jumped around calling me a shrew.

16
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:30,950
I gave him one big boot
and sent him flying.

17
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:32,680
Scared the crap out of him—
he took off running.

18
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:33,789
We agreed

19
00:01:33,789 --> 00:01:35,090
we'd never see each other
again in this life.

20
00:01:35,090 --> 00:01:36,250
Whoever chickens out is a bastard!

21
00:01:36,479 --> 00:01:38,190
Look—look at what he wrote.

22
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:41,039
"By bastard, Sun Zheng."

23
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:43,310
Well, at least he's self-aware.

24
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:46,350
Juan, well...

25
00:01:46,350 --> 00:01:47,479
Calm down.

26
00:01:47,479 --> 00:01:48,410
I can't calm down!

27
00:01:48,710 --> 00:01:49,650
Why should I calm down?

28
00:01:49,650 --> 00:01:51,420
Pies and bricks might fall from the sky,

29
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:52,640
but a kid? Seriously?

30
00:01:53,890 --> 00:01:55,289
He's up to his neck in debt,
nowhere to turn.

31
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:56,300
What's that got to do with me?

32
00:01:56,789 --> 00:01:58,090
Why should I raise his kid for him?

33
00:01:58,160 --> 00:01:58,970
And worse—

34
00:02:00,650 --> 00:02:02,350
raising that homewrecker's kid.

35
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:08,400
I'm so mad.

36
00:02:14,130 --> 00:02:14,870
What?

37
00:02:19,650 --> 00:02:21,000
Why give me the household register?

38
00:02:22,190 --> 00:02:24,020
You want to be on my family register?
Not a chance.

39
00:02:37,650 --> 00:02:39,220
July 13th.

40
00:02:39,780 --> 00:02:41,530
"Love grows over time," my ass.

41
00:02:42,020 --> 00:02:43,800
So he got her pregnant
as soon as he got to Guangzhou.

42
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:47,190
No wonder he wanted to divorce me.

43
00:02:49,970 --> 00:02:50,560
He...

44
00:02:51,130 --> 00:02:52,740
He played me for a fool.

45
00:02:55,270 --> 00:02:55,980
Juan.

46
00:02:59,250 --> 00:03:00,300
What?

47
00:03:00,930 --> 00:03:01,840
What's this?

48
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:07,190
Your name is Qianqian?

49
00:03:09,890 --> 00:03:11,260
Your dad doesn't even want you anymore.

50
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:12,530
He just dumped you here with me.

51
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:14,130
What do you want?

52
00:03:14,710 --> 00:03:16,280
What are you saying?

53
00:03:17,410 --> 00:03:18,740
What are you grunting about?

54
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:20,380
You think I'm a pig?

55
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:22,710
Hello, I'm Qianqian.

56
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:25,090
Hasn't the whole country
standardized Mandarin?

57
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:26,930
What language is that?

58
00:03:26,930 --> 00:03:27,900
Cantonese.

59
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:30,020
That's how they talk in movies.

60
00:03:40,590 --> 00:03:44,130
[Gangzi Restaurant
Go upstairs]

61
00:04:12,890 --> 00:04:13,950
What would you like to eat, sir?

62
00:04:14,740 --> 00:04:15,770
A plate of dumplings.

63
00:04:16,209 --> 00:04:17,000
What filling?

64
00:04:17,810 --> 00:04:18,500
Pickled cabbage.

65
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:20,130
Okay, wait a moment.

66
00:04:23,890 --> 00:04:24,510
Here.

67
00:04:24,830 --> 00:04:26,430
Pickled cabbage dumplings.

68
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:29,600
Two skewers on the house.

69
00:04:29,630 --> 00:04:30,780
-Thank you.
-Here, chopsticks.

70
00:04:31,070 --> 00:04:32,060
Enjoy your meal.

71
00:05:24,870 --> 00:05:25,900
Don't you recognize me?

72
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:27,870
Dude.

73
00:05:33,659 --> 00:05:34,920
Your name's Liu Yang,

74
00:05:35,659 --> 00:05:36,450
right?

75
00:05:37,470 --> 00:05:40,070
We met at the station before.

76
00:05:42,830 --> 00:05:43,600
You

77
00:05:44,390 --> 00:05:45,540
were with

78
00:05:45,860 --> 00:05:46,630
Lin,

79
00:05:47,159 --> 00:05:47,800
Biaozi,

80
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:48,870
and Maodan back then,

81
00:05:49,220 --> 00:05:49,860
right?

82
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:57,350
Who would've thought?

83
00:05:59,250 --> 00:06:00,830
The whole crew died

84
00:06:01,810 --> 00:06:03,450
in that mountain fire.

85
00:06:06,850 --> 00:06:07,850
And you were

86
00:06:08,860 --> 00:06:10,190
the only one who survived.

87
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:20,290
I watched you

88
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:21,310
for a long time over there.

89
00:06:22,310 --> 00:06:23,850
I thought I saw a ghost.

90
00:06:28,890 --> 00:06:30,010
I'm Zhao Changyou.

91
00:06:32,890 --> 00:06:34,640
When you become a ghost,
don't come after us.

92
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:36,520
It's Zhao Changyou
who wants to get rid of you.

93
00:06:36,890 --> 00:06:37,950
We're all friends here.

94
00:06:46,930 --> 00:06:48,810
Sir, another bottle of wine,

95
00:06:49,180 --> 00:06:50,180
and two more dishes.

96
00:06:55,180 --> 00:06:58,550
[Yuhong Square Police Station]

97
00:06:58,920 --> 00:06:59,690
This kid

98
00:06:59,890 --> 00:07:01,390
is really adorable.

99
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:05,930
Isn't she?

100
00:07:06,140 --> 00:07:07,300
She's a spitting image

101
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:08,920
of her vixen mother.

102
00:07:17,350 --> 00:07:19,350
Her dad's got some nerve,

103
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:23,450
leaving the child he had
with his current wife

104
00:07:23,470 --> 00:07:24,820
to his ex-wife.

105
00:07:27,150 --> 00:07:28,330
I'm a police officer.

106
00:07:28,330 --> 00:07:29,620
You think I'd abuse a kid?

107
00:07:30,330 --> 00:07:31,330
Of course not.

108
00:07:31,330 --> 00:07:33,250
Juan, you're beautiful and kind-hearted.

109
00:07:33,250 --> 00:07:35,540
You'll definitely
treat this kid like your own.

110
00:07:35,540 --> 00:07:37,480
Stop sweet-talking me.

111
00:07:38,030 --> 00:07:39,340
I'll call her dad tomorrow

112
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:40,530
to take her away immediately.

113
00:07:40,990 --> 00:07:42,960
Why should I raise the child

114
00:07:43,110 --> 00:07:44,070
born from their illicit affair?

115
00:07:44,250 --> 00:07:45,180
Like I've got nothing better to do?

116
00:07:46,150 --> 00:07:47,780
What if you call him
and he won't take her?

117
00:07:48,150 --> 00:07:49,980
What? You like her?

118
00:07:51,130 --> 00:07:52,640
If you like her, you can raise her.

119
00:07:53,030 --> 00:07:54,070
H-How am I supposed to raise her?

120
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:56,140
[Public Security Monthly Magazine]

121
00:07:55,310 --> 00:07:56,540
I'm a grown man.

122
00:07:56,540 --> 00:07:58,430
M-Me, taking care of a little girl—
how's that gonna look?

123
00:07:59,250 --> 00:08:00,310
If I get married,

124
00:08:00,310 --> 00:08:01,810
I'd definitely want one.

125
00:08:02,370 --> 00:08:03,070
You? Get married?

126
00:08:03,070 --> 00:08:04,180
Your relationship already fell apart.

127
00:08:04,180 --> 00:08:05,180
Who're you gonna marry?

128
00:08:05,180 --> 00:08:06,130
Who're you gonna have a kid with?

129
00:08:06,130 --> 00:08:07,030
Have one yourself?

130
00:08:07,220 --> 00:08:08,060
Do you even have a uterus?

131
00:08:08,060 --> 00:08:10,330
You do. Why didn't you
have a child back then?

132
00:08:14,130 --> 00:08:14,750
Juan,

133
00:08:14,750 --> 00:08:16,430
I-I misspoke.

134
00:08:16,430 --> 00:08:17,230
I didn't mean that.

135
00:08:28,340 --> 00:08:30,350
If I had given birth back then,

136
00:08:31,550 --> 00:08:32,780
the child would be about her age now.

137
00:08:32,799 --> 00:08:34,370
Then why didn't you have one back then?

138
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:38,789
I was mad at my mother-in-law.

139
00:08:38,789 --> 00:08:40,549
She was bedridden at the time,

140
00:08:40,549 --> 00:08:42,580
couldn't move her arms or legs.

141
00:08:42,809 --> 00:08:44,320
She just kept yapping with her mouth,

142
00:08:44,320 --> 00:08:44,980
urging me every day

143
00:08:45,370 --> 00:08:48,000
to carry on the Sun family line.

144
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:48,770
She told me

145
00:08:49,100 --> 00:08:51,740
that a child is the best gift from God.

146
00:08:52,550 --> 00:08:53,700
What did you say?

147
00:08:55,270 --> 00:08:56,130
I told her

148
00:08:56,150 --> 00:08:58,000
that we police officers
have rules against accepting gifts.

149
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:02,070
Juan, you're quite principled.

150
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:04,600
Then a couple of days later,
the old lady passed away.

151
00:09:04,890 --> 00:09:05,960
I was wondering

152
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:07,550
if she died because I pissed her off.

153
00:09:08,750 --> 00:09:09,530
-Juan.
-You know—

154
00:09:10,110 --> 00:09:11,480
Don't take it to heart.

155
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:13,130
It's definitely not karma.

156
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:14,660
What are you talking about?

157
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:15,890
I was trying to say,

158
00:09:16,150 --> 00:09:17,910
that little girl's from the south, right?

159
00:09:18,770 --> 00:09:19,940
Do you think she can get used to eating

160
00:09:19,940 --> 00:09:21,050
pickled cabbage dumplings?

161
00:09:35,670 --> 00:09:36,440
Dude,

162
00:09:37,290 --> 00:09:38,960
I'll be honest with you today.

163
00:09:40,530 --> 00:09:41,720
I've been

164
00:09:42,630 --> 00:09:43,940
in the mountain

165
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:45,530
goods business

166
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:47,250
with Lin and the others

167
00:09:47,820 --> 00:09:48,840
for six or seven years.

168
00:09:49,700 --> 00:09:51,170
They handle the transport,

169
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:52,530
and I handle the sales.

170
00:09:53,770 --> 00:09:54,410
You

171
00:09:55,170 --> 00:09:55,820
might see

172
00:09:56,440 --> 00:09:57,150
that

173
00:09:57,150 --> 00:09:59,720
they do all the hard work,

174
00:10:00,150 --> 00:10:02,120
but I take all the risks.

175
00:10:07,750 --> 00:10:08,630
What do you mean?

176
00:10:10,740 --> 00:10:12,270
Before the wildfire,

177
00:10:12,870 --> 00:10:14,460
they still had a batch of goods

178
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:16,630
stuck up there.

179
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:21,860
They said it was hidden
somewhere in the mountains.

180
00:10:21,860 --> 00:10:23,600
Do you know about it?

181
00:10:29,890 --> 00:10:30,600
Dude,

182
00:10:32,130 --> 00:10:33,440
don't try to fool me.

183
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:39,600
I know exactly how

184
00:10:39,700 --> 00:10:41,340
the three of them died.

185
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:55,030
Before, Lin and I

186
00:10:56,940 --> 00:10:58,030
split it forty-sixty.

187
00:10:59,150 --> 00:11:00,050
I took sixty,

188
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:01,390
and they took forty.

189
00:11:02,550 --> 00:11:04,390
As long as you help me
find this batch of goods,

190
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:07,440
we'll split it fifty-fifty.

191
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:08,980
Deal?

192
00:11:14,530 --> 00:11:15,170
Fine.

193
00:11:17,270 --> 00:11:18,240
Let me tell you

194
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:20,220
one more thing.

195
00:11:23,620 --> 00:11:25,850
I've got a warehouse on Siying Road

196
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,760
with a batch of goods in stock.

197
00:11:30,410 --> 00:11:31,550
If you trust me,

198
00:11:33,740 --> 00:11:35,620
after this batch sells,

199
00:11:36,130 --> 00:11:39,030
we go fifty-fifty too.

200
00:11:55,910 --> 00:11:57,860
What you're doing is illegal, isn't it?

201
00:11:59,770 --> 00:12:00,390
Dude,

202
00:12:01,530 --> 00:12:02,930
fortune favors the bold.

203
00:12:16,700 --> 00:12:17,100
Here.

204
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:18,980
Cheers.

205
00:12:23,010 --> 00:12:23,620
Cheers.

206
00:12:29,950 --> 00:12:32,930
[Yuhong Stadium]

207
00:12:34,150 --> 00:12:35,050
How can such

208
00:12:35,050 --> 00:12:36,890
a little thing pee so much?

209
00:12:37,170 --> 00:12:37,980
Ma Xiangqian.

210
00:12:37,980 --> 00:12:38,600
Coming.

211
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:39,550
Come, carry this out.

212
00:12:39,770 --> 00:12:40,980
Dry it on the stove.

213
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:45,860
If you want to go to the toilet,

214
00:12:45,860 --> 00:12:46,410
just tell me.

215
00:12:46,410 --> 00:12:46,940
You hear me?

216
00:12:49,150 --> 00:12:49,980
Telling you is useless.

217
00:12:49,980 --> 00:12:51,370
You don't understand a thing.

218
00:12:51,790 --> 00:12:53,270
I knew bringing this little one back

219
00:12:53,270 --> 00:12:54,290
would be nothing but trouble.

220
00:12:54,790 --> 00:12:55,390
What?

221
00:12:56,070 --> 00:12:57,720
Back then I scratched your mom,

222
00:12:58,230 --> 00:13:00,040
and now you're here to avenge her?

223
00:13:19,820 --> 00:13:20,600
What?

224
00:13:22,460 --> 00:13:23,550
You want some too?

225
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:28,440
What do you mean?

226
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:29,980
Nodding's yes, shaking's no.

227
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:31,100
And "xie xie ni" means

228
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:32,150
"very much thank you".

229
00:13:32,790 --> 00:13:34,120
You're nodding and shaking your head.

230
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:35,170
How am I supposed to figure it out?

231
00:13:47,050 --> 00:13:48,940
Are you afraid of wetting the bed
so you won't drink water?

232
00:13:51,270 --> 00:13:52,550
It's fine.

233
00:13:52,550 --> 00:13:53,650
I'll get up in two hours

234
00:13:53,650 --> 00:13:54,980
and take you to pee.

235
00:13:55,390 --> 00:13:56,340
Come on, drink.

236
00:13:56,630 --> 00:13:57,770
Drink from this side.

237
00:13:57,770 --> 00:13:58,790
I haven't touched this side.

238
00:13:59,620 --> 00:14:00,290
Okay.

239
00:14:02,510 --> 00:14:03,240
Alright.

240
00:14:04,240 --> 00:14:05,700
There you go. Right?

241
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:06,600
I'll carry you over.

242
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:07,790
God.

243
00:14:07,860 --> 00:14:08,870
You're quite heavy.

244
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:11,170
Lie down here.

245
00:14:11,390 --> 00:14:12,400
These are newly changed.

246
00:14:12,500 --> 00:14:13,390
They're very clean.

247
00:14:14,370 --> 00:14:14,670
Juan.

248
00:14:14,670 --> 00:14:15,080
Your little legs.

249
00:14:15,500 --> 00:14:16,530
Cover her with this. It's thick.

250
00:14:16,530 --> 00:14:16,980
Okay.

251
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:19,750
We've been up half the night.

252
00:14:32,840 --> 00:14:33,740
Do you smell that?

253
00:14:34,770 --> 00:14:36,370
What's that smell? Something's burning.

254
00:14:37,940 --> 00:14:38,910
I'm drying the clothes.

255
00:14:39,650 --> 00:14:40,220
Oh my.

256
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:42,150
You can't do anything right.

257
00:14:42,150 --> 00:14:42,970
Look at you.

258
00:14:43,650 --> 00:14:44,240
Fire!

259
00:14:44,440 --> 00:14:45,760
You two really don't give me a break!

260
00:14:45,980 --> 00:14:46,820
One sets a fire.

261
00:14:46,820 --> 00:14:48,150
And the other pees there.

262
00:14:48,700 --> 00:14:49,570
You're gonna kill me.
